{
  "id": "queue-loop-wait-before-stop",
  "title": "Goal reached with learning cards still due today: reviewing, then waiting, and goal_reached only when nothing is left for today (ADR-049)",
  "covers": [
    "queue.loop_waits_before_stop"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "The case reported on 2026-11-19, scaled down (9 ready / 14 later / 707 new there; 1 / 2 / 2 here). scheduler.reviews_unlimited is true, new_per_day is 3. Cards ...10, ...20 and ...30 were introduced today and answered Again at 09:59:00, 09:59:55 and 09:59:58: they are in the first learning step (60 s) and fall due at 10:00:00, 10:00:55 and 10:00:58. The goal is reached (3/3). No review is due. Cards ...40 and ...50 are new.",
    "Step 0, 10:00:01: ...10 is ready, two are later today. reviewing, never goal_reached; until_stop 3 = until_stop_parts 1 learning + 2 later + 0 reviews + 0 new, the numbers the header and Home show; keep_going_available is false because a card is served.",
    "Step 1 graduates ...10 (Easy). Step 2, 10:00:03: nothing is ready, two learning cards fall due later today and new cards remain. Under ADR-037 this was goal_reached; under ADR-049 it is waiting with next_due_at 10:00:55, keep_going_available true, until_stop 2. No card is served early. The deprecated more_available is true and next_learning_due_at is set, as before.",
    "Step 3, the same instant with keep_going=true&limit=1: reviewing with the new card ...40 (the learning cards are not served early); until_stop 0 + 2 + 0 + 1 = 3; keep_going_available false; ready, later_today, backlog, reviews and new equal step 2.",
    "Step 4, 10:00:55, without the flag (a new visit, or the timer of rule C4/C6): ...20 came due and is served: reviewing, 1 learning + 1 later.",
    "Step 5 graduates ...20. Step 6, 10:00:57: waiting again for ...30 (next_due_at 10:00:58), until_stop 1.",
    "Step 7, 10:00:58: ...30 is served. Step 8 graduates it.",
    "Step 9, 10:01:00: nothing is ready and nothing falls due later today: only now goal_reached, with until_stop 0, all four parts 0 and keep_going_available true.",
    "Step 10, keep_going=true&limit=1: reviewing with the new card ...40; the mode-independent numbers equal step 9."
  ],
